, so it is visually\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:58:# - Exactly one near-center 6x6 thick cross exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:152:def _find_cross_hub(g: np.ndarray, bg: int):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:157:            # The four 2x2 corners must be background so the 6x6 bbox visibly reads as a cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:232:    hub = _find_cross_hub(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/0/code.py:230:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/3/code.py:146:    - Mirror the whole sprite across that axis. Originals and red controls remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:13:#       Each target is an interior crosshair:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:15:#       - one short perpendicular tick crossing the rail,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:16:#       - a colored center pixel at the crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:33:#       A horizontal rail on row 6 with crosshair center at (6, 9) means the marker must end\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:36:#       so the generator switches to one sprite per crosshair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:46:#       shared orientation. The dataset still varies orientation across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:50:#       - \"anchor is an isolated singleton\": false now, because the center is embedded in a crosshair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:72:#       - crosshair centers as the destinations,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:78:#     That avoids clutter near the rails and keeps the new crosshair cue unambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:92:    Slide multi-color sprites along interior crosshair rails until their marker pixels reach the matching centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:96:    - One or more interior crosshairs: a long monochrome rail plus a short perpendicular tick, with a colored center pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:97:    - Multi-color sprites whose minority-color marker matches one crosshair center color; only the marker sits on that rail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:100:    - Detect each crosshair by its long rail, then match sprites to the center pixel sharing the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:104:    Key insight: The long internal line, not the border, now encodes the motion axis and target location; the colored crossing pixel is the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D1/0/code.py:58:#    cross the masked edge row/column. The transformed variants are produced by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:43:- `placeholder_colors` used to come from one crop. Now colors must be aggregated across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:90:    total blocks across all frames: 6-10\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:165:    Key insight: The external clues are still global, but the placeholders are partitioned across several independent frames, so the solver must first assign each color to the correct frame before stamping the sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/0/code.py:36:#         across the strip thickness: left border in a vertical strip, top border in a horizontal strip;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/0/code.py:54:#     - the target palette is small (3 colors per sample) and reused across many holes, which avoids a noisy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/1/code.py:185:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/2/code.py:91:    Every non-red, non-background 4-connected component is mirrored across it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/0/code.py:60:#    slots share the same color. This makes the change visible across only a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/0/code.py:117:    Sort vertical bars by height and redistribute them across fixed x-slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D8/0/code.py:354:        # Now verify exactly 1 valid attachment across all 4 rotations x 4 sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D8/0/code.py:358:        # We need exactly 1 such (rotation, side) pair across all possibilities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:41:#      local regularities across examples rather than too many degrees of freedom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:66:#    - Across examples, horizontal lines yield tall stacked outputs; vertical lines\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:79:#         * one full straight separator line across the canvas\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:15:#      outline around an irregular enclosed region shaped like an L or a cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:23:#      corner of that 4 x 4 box lies outside the L/cross interior, those sprite pixels\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:26:#    - Shape family is limited to two visible categories: L and cross. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:39:#      interior mask or they would leak across the missing corners / arms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:42:#      intersection with the interior is 4-connected, non-empty, and still spans the full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:47:#    - At least one placeholder is visibly truncated by the L/cross boundary, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:366:    \"\"\"Return valid slot boxes whose intersection with the irregular interior stays bbox-sized.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:395:    \"\"\"Build an L or cross interior mask whose valid slot count stays in range.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:398:        shape_type = random.choice([\"L\", \"cross\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:400:        if shape_type == \"cross\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:48:#     - Anchor colors stay limited to 1-3 and are reused across 3-5 sprites, so each sample\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:72:#     - The generator mixes top/bottom and left/right anchors and reuses colors across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D8/1/code.py:26:#       This keeps the visual effect obvious across 2-4 examples without introducing arbitrary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D13/1/code.py:57:    non-local comparison across multiple candidate regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/2/code.py:211:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:28:#      repeated marker color per grid and splits that color across both anchors of its pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:49:#    - Because at least one color is reused and split across both anchors, the \"choose nearer\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:50:#      branch is usually demonstrated within a single grid instead of relying only on cross-grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:29:#      Input may contain 4 bars crossing the baseline plus 2 floating 2x2 blocks in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:32:#      components crossing the baseline and matching the solid centered-rectangle bar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:60:#    - Across 2-4 examples, humans can see that the corner/edge blocks never move\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:61:#      while only the baseline-crossing bars get permuted by height. That difference\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:104:    - Ignore foreground distractor blocks that do not match the baseline-crossing bar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:106:    - Sort only the true bars by height and redistribute them across the original\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:16:#   chamber, so stamping a sprite cannot cross the divider. The left chamber and the right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:28:#   targets across the two regions, making the partition visually consequential.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:44:#   chamber walls, so no sprite can touch or cross the divider after stamping.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:171:            assert len(regs) == 1 and -1 not in regs, f\"placeholder color {col} crosses a divider\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/2/code.py:334:            assert int(region_by_cell[rr, cc]) == ridx, f\"sprite for color {src_col} crosses the divider\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D15/2/code.py:59:#    - The four marker corners are used repeatedly across a sample, and the rectangular cores\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D5/0/code.py:26:#     the formerly disappearing quadrant now remains near the split intersection and turns green\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D1/1/code.py:75:# - The repeated cross-example pattern is visible: the sprite above moves to the top,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/3/code.py:52:  - Only one shared color is reused across the three chained groups. This is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/3/code.py:54:    color per group\" habit would suppress all cross-stage interactions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/3/code.py:94:  - The only color adaptation is controlled color sharing across the three linked\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/3/code.py:96:    reused across stages.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/3/code.py:60:#      least one marker color across small and large regions. Humans can therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/3/code.py:233:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:28:- Across the dataset, the adjacent-side pair varies, so the multi-opening rule is still visually\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:52:  output shows one straight beam per gap. Because openings span both axes across the dataset,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D1/1/code.py:332:    # Add a 1-cell-deep interior brace across one gap so the wall stays connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D1/0/code.py:21:#   on the top row. Input bars are permuted across the existing x-slots; output moves\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D1/0/code.py:43:# - Visual observability: across 2-4 examples a human can track that every color moves\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D1/0/code.py:112:    - Several monochrome vertical bars cross the base line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:42:#     split across both vertical and horizontal pairings so the variant is observable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:175:    - Outside the frame: one sprite template per placeholder color, and legend fragments spread across the grid edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D7/1/code.py:176:    - Each legend entry is split across opposite edges: the top/left fragment shows the source symbol, while the opposite bottom/right fragment shows only the output color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:44:#    Because the same palette reappears across several separated regions, a human\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:52:#    keeps the shared palette short enough to notice, while repeated use across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D8/2/code.py:124:    - Gather all marker colors across the entire grid in row-major order, keeping the first occurrence of each color to form one global palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:10:    embedded_cross:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:17:        The payload is copied into the other three quadrants: mirror across the horizontal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:18:        axis, mirror across the vertical axis, and point reflection around the same center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:39:    - To keep the rule learnable, the cross is always the same exact 5-pixel shape; arm\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:41:    - Every generated grid contains at least one embedded cross, and larger grids often have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:60:        so the three generated copies never overlap the original or the red cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:67:      mistaken for embedded crosses.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:69:    - A human can see the exact same cross shape paired with one occupied quadrant in input\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:70:      and all four quadrants in output across multiple examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:77:    - Marker red is reserved for the cross or isolated point only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D8/2/code.py:390:            \"kind\": \"embedded_cross\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D12/0/code.py:96:  marker at the edge-line intersection before any whole-grid transform.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D1/1/c