s multiple objects when possible so the legend is not a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D15/0/code.py:58:  object across the training distribution.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2ba387bc/D15/0/code.py:91:  they never cross the legend boundary or the outer grid boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:3:# Change: 交叉标记（crossing markers）——垂直管道通过水平管道的交叉处，用一对5号像素标记穿行管道的交叉点前后，表示'直行不转弯'；9号矩形块作为宽接合体直穿对面\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:9:#     original: horizontal crossover rows place grey 5-cells on both sides of any vertical wire that should pass straight through the row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:10:#     new: remove those 5-cells entirely. Crossings are plain cyan '+' intersections. When a routed signal reaches such a 4-way junction,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:16:#       - A real crossing is a bare 8-colored plus: the center cell has 4 wire neighbors and no grey side markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:19:#       - Wire layout stays fixed, but all examples containing crossings now show unmarked '+' junctions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:22:#       - A token enters a vertical wire from above and reaches a row where a horizontal swap segment crosses it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:24:#       - The crossing row contained 5,8,5 around the vertical column, explicitly hinting that the vertical path continues through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:29:#       - Output is still the same channel permutation, but the input no longer carries per-crossing marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:32:#     - Reject generated layouts without at least one visible bare crossing, otherwise D2 would not be observable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:33:#     - Do not add extra crossing subtypes; a single deterministic priority rule is enough and avoids underconstrained examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:44:#     - After embedding rectangles, the generator rechecks that at least one visible crossing remains outside rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:46:#     - Humans can compare examples and notice that crossing rows no longer contain grey brackets even when multiple swaps exist.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:47:#     - Bare '+' intersections are visually simpler than the old 5-bracket motif, but requiring at least one exposed crossing keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:167:    At an unmarked '+' crossing, keep moving straight if possible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:239:    - Bare wire crossings have no grey markers: when a path reaches a four-way '+' junction, it continues straight ahead whenever that forward edge exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:242:    - The missing crossing markers mean routing must be inferred from connectivity plus travel direction: keep the current heading through plain '+' intersections and pass straight across 9-blocks when the opposite face is available.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:356:def _decompose_to_crossovers(perm):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:357:    \"\"\"Decompose a permutation into sequential crossover moves using the bypass column.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:360:    crossovers = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:373:        crossovers.append((cycle[0], -1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:375:            crossovers.append((cycle[k], cycle[(k + 1) % len(cycle)]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:376:        crossovers.append((-1, cycle[1]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:377:    return crossovers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:386:def _count_visible_crossings(grid: np.ndarray) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:387:    \"\"\"Count exposed color-8 '+' intersections with all four orthogonal neighbors also color 8.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:407:        mode = \"crossing\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:430:    if mode == \"crossing\" and xover_rows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:481:def _build_wire_network(grid, n_channels, ch_cols, bypass_col, top_ep_row, bot_ep_row, crossovers, xover_rows):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:482:    \"\"\"Draw the wire network onto grid. Returns (slot_wire, bypass_wire) after all crossovers.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:491:    for xover_idx, (src_slot, dst_slot) in enumerate(crossovers):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:590:    crossovers = _decompose_to_crossovers(perm)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:591:    n_xovers = len(crossovers)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:616:        grid, n_channels, ch_cols, bypass_col, top_ep_row, bot_ep_row, crossovers, xover_rows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:618:    if _count_visible_crossings(grid) < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D2/1/code.py:636:    if _count_visible_crossings(grid) < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7666fa5d/D5/1/code.py:31:      - always starting from red on the leftmost visible gap gives a stable, learnable pattern across 2-4 examples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:24:#    same topology can recolor differently across regions, and a hole count valid in one region can be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:32:#    The generator draws a cross of full-span d