ound marker color and paint that color across the entire right side on every row covered by the cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b5ca7ac4/D13/1/code.py:21:#      right-moving group. The swatch colors swap across generated examples, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D5/0/code.py:50:#   stamp fits after clipping. Row/col marks remain unique across mover colors, reducing ambiguity in target matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D5/0/code.py:57:# - Across only 2-4 examples, a human can now see three repeated cues for each mover color:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D5/0/code.py:61:#   switch that would require more examples to infer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:41:#    Every generated sample contains at least one bounce, and bounced rays keep crossing beside walls whose color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:42:#    differs from the ray color. Across 2-4 examples this should make the new rule legible: walls redirect rays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:23:#   1. a large cross: full middle row + full middle column (9 cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:26:#   the resting shape (large cross), while the missing complement (corner-star)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:28:#   large cross to the far endpoint. A pre-placed large cross is already stable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:31:#   variant: solid 5x5 at top -> top large cross, bottom corner-star\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:36:# - The two complementary results are still few and repeated across channels:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:37:#   every sample shows several large crosses and several corner-stars, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:39:# - The corner-star is disconnected under 4-connectivity, while the cross is\n/home