 which keeps the edge coding clean. Stamps are\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:27:#      cross one edge or one corner. That is visually obvious without introducing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:35:#    - Offsets `r in [0, 20-H]`, `c in [0, 20-W]` assumed the crop never crossed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:44:#      with at least one crossed edge. The crop is never fully outside the motif.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:51:#    - Samples vary between single-edge and corner crossings so the boundary cue is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:189:    - Use the border-colored cells to recover the rectangular in-bounds part of the crop, which reveals which sides of the 20x20 support were crossed and sharply narrows the allowed source offsets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:205:def _sample_crossing_sides(rng: random.Random) -> tuple[str, ...]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D17/2/code.py:248:        sides = _sample_crossing_sides(rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D2/3/code.py:36:#    masks are explicitly asymmetric, so horizontal/vertical/180-degree changes are obvious across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/fc7cae8d/D10/0/code.py:46:#    Across examples, humans can now see several interior rectangles. Only one rectangle carries the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D11/0/code.py:65:#   share the minority geometry, but their dominant color switches to the other\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D11/1/code.py:34:    - keep colors distinct and row/col marks non-reused across movers to avoid ambiguous matching\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D11/1/code.py:48:    - reused row/col marks are forbidden across movers, as in the original task\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D11/1/code.py:49:    - median target rows/cols are also kept distinct across movers so single-target placements are less\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D11/1/code.py:58:      and columns across movers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D11/1/code.py:122:      intersection. Bottom-to-top covering order is unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D11/1/code.py:243:    The resulting median target must not be reused across movers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D1/2/code.py:25:#    - Grouping frames by `inner` color no longer holds, so grouping must switch to a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D1/2/code.py:31:#      line and bridge across the overlap of the two inner bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D1/2/code.py:33:#      outside a smaller target's opening. The variant uses the intersection band, i.e. the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D1/2/code.py:34:#      common visible opening across the pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D1/2/code.py:37:#    computes bridges on the intended path, rejects overlaps/crossings, and verifies the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D8/0/code.py:17:# rectangular cell interiors whose height and width both vary across samples. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b99e7126/D8/0/code.py:90:    - Slide that mask across the coarse cell grid until the visible minority cells fit in exactly one place,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D13/1/code.py:30:#    mover, and no row/col mark reuse across movers. To make D13 visible, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D13/0/code.py:225:    read marker-defined target intersections exactly as in the original task,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:19:#    (4,2). The crossing area is a 2x2 background patch inside an empty lattice cell. Under the old\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D13/0/code.py:31:#    Long bridges are allowed only across empty lattice rows/columns. The generator rejects any scene\n/home/lixinyu/sna